    <p style="text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;color:#52d6b2;font-weight:800;">System FAQ</p>
    <h1 style="font-size:3rem;line-height:1.08;margin:12px 0;">ZeroThink FAQ</h1>
    <details open style="border:1px solid #26303a;border-radius:8px;margin:14px 0;padding:16px;">
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;color:#fff;font-weight:800;">How does ZeroThink support academic literature research?</summary>
        <p style="color:#a5b0ba;">ZeroThink provides research-facing workflows for literature discovery, survey extension, topic-expert identification, generative UI, provenance tracking, and researcher-controlled validation.</p>
        <p style="color:#a5b0ba;">The literature workspace helps researchers move from a broad topic to a structured evidence map, source ledger, expert/topic view, review extension, and carefully bounded AI-assisted synthesis.</p>
        <p style="color:#a5b0ba;">A literature-research plugin, repository invitation, or university project is not automatically the same thing as an integrated ZeroThink agent feature. The site does not claim institutional adoption, invitation, availability, or endorsement without documented confirmation.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border:1px solid #26303a;border-radius:8px;margin:14px 0;padding:16px;">
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;color:#fff;font-weight:800;">Does ZeroThink expose hidden chain-of-thought?</summary>
        <p style="color:#a5b0ba;">No. Custom research process options are visible scaffolds, checklists, stages, rubrics, validation checks, and workflow templates.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border:1px solid #26303a;border-radius:8px;margin:14px 0;padding:16px;">
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;color:#fff;font-weight:800;">How does OpenZero work inside ZeroThink?</summary>
        <p style="color:#a5b0ba;">OpenZero Local is a Pro lane for small self-hosted models under 15 GB. When the shared gateway is enabled, Pro accounts can use 5 shared ZeroThink OpenZero messages, then should install OpenZero and save their own OpenZero Machine API Key through a server-side registered gateway.</p>
        <p style="color:#a5b0ba;">Featherless is separate: it is a hosted large-model lane for TalkToAI ZERO, GLM 5.2, GLM 4.5, Qwen3 Coder, DeepSeek, and Kimi, using the user's own Featherless key.</p>
    </details>
    <p><a href="/nottingham-research" style="color:#52d6b2;">Open Literature Research Workspace</a></p>
</section>
